# The caves of Alola: a long way under the island, water dripping into dark pools and every sound coming back a moment
# late. A harp turning a minor chord over and over in C, high drips of a celesta at no particular time, a low warm pad and a
# bowed bass, an ocarina wandering in from the middle, a bell that tolls the root now and then and a timpani far off. The same
# by day and night, as the caves keep no hours.
# Original composition for this game, in the modern sound.
title Cave (Alola)
tempo 72
meter 4/4
reverb 0.42
night none
room hall 3.4

